{"prdMarkdown":"# PRD: Client-Side Form Validation for Signup Form\n\n## Problem Statement\nUsers registering for the internal operations dashboard need immediate, clear feedback on form inputs to prevent submission errors and reduce registration friction. Currently, the repository (`README.md`, `package.json`) does not contain a signup form component, route, or client-side validation logic.\n\n## Goals\n- Provide real-time, inline validation feedback as users enter their registration details.\n- Prevent invalid submissions from reaching the backend, minimizing unnecessary API requests.\n- Present clear, actionable error messages for each input field.\n- Seamlessly handle both client-side validation states and server-side responses (e.g., duplicate account conflicts).\n\n## Non-goals\n- Modifying backend authentication or validation logic in `src/api/client.js`.\n- Implementing multi-step onboarding or profile completion flows.\n- Redesigning existing navigation components such as `src/components/Header.jsx`.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers will receive immediate visual confirmation when inputs meet requirements (e.g., valid email formatting, password strength) and clear guidance when inputs fail validation, leading to fewer failed registration attempts.\n\n## Open Product Questions\n- **Signup Form Scope**: Confirm whether building the entire signup form UI, routing, and submission flow from scratch is within scope for this request, as no registration screen currently exists in `src/App.jsx`.\n- **Field Requirements**: What specific fields are required on the signup form (e.g., email, password, confirm password, name), and what are the exact validation rules (e.g., minimum password length, special characters)?\n- **Error Timing UX**: Should inline errors trigger immediately on the first keystroke, or should they be suppressed until a field has been blurred (visited) to avoid aggressive premature validation warnings while the user is still actively typing?","trdMarkdown":"# TRD: Client-Side Form Validation Implementation\n\n## Architecture Notes\n- **Routing & Component Structure**: The project currently uses React 18 and React Router DOM v6 (`package.json`). A new signup route and component (e.g., `src/pages/Signup.jsx` or `src/components/SignupForm.jsx`) will need to be introduced and wired into `src/App.jsx`.\n- **Form State & Validation**: Existing dependencies in `package.json` are limited to `react` and `react-router-dom`. Validation can either be implemented using custom React state hooks managing `values`, `errors`, and `touched` states, or by adding lightweight external libraries (such as React Hook Form or Zod).\n- **API Integration**: Submission logic must interface with `src/api/client.js` to dispatch registration requests and catch backend rejection responses (e.g., 400 validation failures, 409 conflict errors for duplicate emails) to map back to field-level or form-level error states.\n\n## Edge Cases & Dependencies\n- **Premature Validation on Initial Keystroke**: Running validation on every keystroke on an unvisited field can produce premature errors (such as showing \"Invalid email\" after typing the first character). Tracking `touched` or `dirty` state per field is required to ensure smooth UX.\n- **Dependency Footprint**: `package.json` currently has no form management dependencies. Introducing external schema validation or form libraries requires evaluation against bundle size and architectural preferences.\n- **Asynchronous & Server Errors**: Backend errors returned via `src/api/client.js` (e.g., network timeout, duplicate account) must be displayed gracefully without wiping valid user inputs.\n\n## Engineering Questions\n- Should validation logic be implemented using custom React state/hooks, or should dependencies like `react-hook-form` or `zod` be added to `package.json`?\n- What are the endpoint specifications, payload shapes, and error response formats in `src/api/client.js` for user registration?\n\n## Estimate\n- Nominal: 2-5 days\n- Worst case: Up to 10 days (accounting for building the entire signup form UI, routing, and server-side error mapping from scratch)"}